From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sf2000-linux <sf2000-linux@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mips: sf2000: enable interrupt-driven WAIT idle

The initial trap bring-up skipped check_wait() while exception and interrupt
delivery were still unproven.  That leaves cpu_wait NULL permanently, so the
idle task spins on this single-core CPU and QEMU consumes a complete host core
even after the guest has settled.

The SF2000 CPU profile is deliberately CPU_4KC and the timer/exception paths
are now covered by retained physical logs and emulator smoke tests.  Select
the standard r4k_wait implementation after vectors are installed.  The
existing `nowait` kernel option remains an immediate recovery switch for
hardware variants whose WAIT implementation is defective.
---
 arch/mips/kernel/traps.c | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/mips/kernel/traps.c b/arch/mips/kernel/traps.c
index a6eef4646..e1b7fbbe0 100644
--- a/arch/mips/kernel/traps.c
+++ b/arch/mips/kernel/traps.c
@@ -2488,8 +2488,7 @@ void __init trap_init(void)
 	unsigned long i, vec_size;
 	phys_addr_t ebase_pa;
 
-	if (!IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_MIPS_SF2000))
-		check_wait();
+	check_wait();
 	sf2000_trap_tick("trap-after-check-wait");
 
 	if (!cpu_has_mips_r2_r6) {
-- 
2.49.0
